  "inlineSchema": "// The Account registries schema — STRICTLY the Canonical Persistence Model\n// (RC-1), reference: adapters-persistence-identity. The engine is a\n// mechanism (S-1); the R-A key of the Subscription lives in the\n// hand-authored migration SQL as a PARTIAL UNIQUE INDEX (the migration is\n// the truth of the DDL).\n//\n// JUSTIFIED DIVERGENCES from the reference (Domain Checklist §I):\n// - ONE context-wide fact-stream/outbox/inbox (AccountFact/AccountOutbox/\n//   AccountInbox) keyed by `subjectKey` (the unit's identity: personId for\n//   Account and AvailabilityFrame facts, subscriptionId for Subscription\n//   facts) instead of per-unit table sets: THREE units publish here where\n//   Identity had ONE — per-subject order (F4.3 §4) is exactly the\n//   (subjectKey, sequence) key, and the relay claims by subjectKey either\n//   way. Same laws, fewer tables, one relay source.\n// - The CHOREOGRAPHY STORE tables (RFC-003 P3/P4): the journey's Inbox,\n//   position and Outbox de commandes — Identity has no ratified reaction;\n//   Account's choreography is canon (\"chorégraphie interne\").\n// - NO SupportRequest fact/outbox/inbox tables: state-only by ABSENCE\n//   (precedent: Session). The absence is the proof.\n\n// Generator `prisma-client` (ESM TypeScript into src/generated) — same\n// collision-free door as the reference (a default-output generation would\n// overwrite the shared store's Agreement client).\ngenerator client {\n  provider               = \"prisma-client\"\n  output                 = \"../src/generated/prisma\"\n  moduleFormat           = \"esm\"\n  generatedFileExtension = \"ts\"\n  importFileExtension    = \"js\"\n}\n\ndatasource db {\n  provider = \"postgresql\"\n  url      = env(\"MENTORA_ACCOUNT_DATABASE_URL\")\n}\n\n// RC-1 §1/§2 — the PRIVATE photographs: one row per unit, version =\n// optimistic guard (F5.2 §4; version law of this context: +1 per act).\n// stateKind / reachability / verificationState materialize the read\n// adapters' walks — derived from the photograph, never a second truth.\nmodel AccountSnapshot {\n  personId          String  @id\n  version           Int\n  payload           String\n  checksum          String\n  stateKind         String\n  verificationState String\n  reachability      String?\n\n  @@index([stateKind])\n}\n\n// Singleton-par-Compte (RFC-003 P2): the frame's identity IS the person's.\nmodel AvailabilityFrameSnapshot {\n  personId String @id\n  version  Int\n  payload  String\n  checksum String\n}\n\n// The R-A key \"une souscription active par titulaire\" is the PARTIAL UNIQUE\n// INDEX subscription_active_holder_ra_key (migration SQL; WHERE stateKind =\n// 'Active' ON personId) — declared by the domain's specification, applied\n// structurally at retention, refused as SubscriptionAlreadyExists.\nmodel SubscriptionSnapshot {\n  subscriptionId String @id\n  version        Int\n  payload        String\n  checksum       String\n  personId       String\n  stateKind      String\n\n  @@index([personId, stateKind])\n}\n\n// STATE ONLY — no fact table, no outbox, no inbox exists for this unit.\nmodel SupportRequestSnapshot {\n  supportRequestId String @id\n  version          Int\n  payload          String\n  checksum         String\n  stateKind        String\n}\n\n// RC-1 §3 — the append-only fact stream of the CONTEXT: EventIdentity =\n// (subjectKey, sequence); wire payload of the published language (V-1);\n// no UPDATE, no DELETE (S-9). Order is per unit subject only (F4.3 §4).\nmodel AccountFact {\n  subjectKey      String\n  sequence        Int\n  type            String\n  payload         String\n  contractVersion Int\n  occurredAtMs    BigInt\n  checksum        String\n\n  @@id([subjectKey, sequence])\n}\n\n// RC-1 §4 — the Outbox de faits, born in the SAME atomic retention (A-3);\n// correlation/causation from the RetentionContext (RFC-001) when they exist.\nmodel AccountOutbox {\n  id               BigInt  @id @default(autoincrement())\n  messageId        String  @unique\n  subjectKey       String\n  sequence         Int\n  correlationId    String?\n  causationId      String?\n  deliveryAttempts Int     @default(0)\n  payload          String\n  occurredAtMs     BigInt\n  status           String  @default(\"pending\")\n  claimedUntilMs   BigInt  @default(0)\n  nextAttemptAtMs  BigInt  @default(0)\n  quarantineReason String?\n\n  @@unique([subjectKey, sequence])\n  @@index([status, id])\n}\n\n// RC-1 §5 — the per-CONSUMER register of processed fact identities (M-4).\nmodel AccountInbox {\n  consumer      String\n  subjectKey    String\n  sequence      Int\n  processedAtMs BigInt\n\n  @@id([consumer, subjectKey, sequence])\n}\n\n// ---- The DECLARED choreography's store (RFC-003 P3/P4) ----------------\n// The journey's own Inbox (fact identities it retained), its POSITION (the\n// only memory a journey may have — the pardon test) and its Outbox de\n// commandes (drained by the composition's declared handler).\n\nmodel ChoreographyInbox {\n  factIdentity String @id\n  retainedAtMs BigInt\n}\n\nmodel ChoreographyPosition {\n  journeyKey String @id\n  // VersionedPayload of ChoreographyPosition (canonical JSON).\n  payload    String\n  checksum   String\n}\n\nmodel ChoreographyCommand {\n  id        BigInt @id @default(autoincrement())\n  commandId String @unique\n  payload   String\n\n  @@index([id])\n}\n",
